# Ledger row #6 — Memory, L2 — HIP allocator fragmentation env var
# File: run scripts (env var, no source code change)
# Verdict: KEPT (zero-cost), but +3.1% measured (noise-level, no real win)
#
# Targets HIP caching-allocator fragmentation from PyG's variable per-sample
# graph shapes -- a different mechanism than the already-confirmed-inert
# pin_memory/NUMA levers (MI300A's unified CPU+GPU HBM makes those
